title TUI and CLI Capability Migration Boundary
left to right direction
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

' Source evidence (CampusClaw PR 167 f60cc3e against d649866):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/command
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/modes
' Observed behavior: the deleted package tree also owned compaction and Slash Command logic.
' Architecture change: classify by responsibility before deleting a product entry point.
' Design reason: shared session behavior must survive while terminal-only behavior is removed.

rectangle "Former TUI and CLI tree" as Old
package "Replace with HTTP command module" {
  [Definition and composite registry] as Slash
  [Builtin and Skill handlers] as Handlers
  [Narrow application services] as Port
}
package "Move to common session" {
  [Threshold compaction] as Threshold
  [STOP preserve and error overflow one retry] as Overflow
  [Read file tracker] as Tracker
}
package "Delete" {
  [TUI components and launchers] as Tui
  [Interactive OneShot RPC ACP] as Modes
  [JSONL auth settings tree] as Local
  [Import export clipboard editor templates] as Terminal
  [PackageManager extensions themes shortcuts] as Packages
  [Loop OS cron installer notifications] as Legacy
}

Old --> Slash : keep
Slash --> Handlers
Handlers --> Port
Old --> Threshold : move
Old --> Overflow : move
Old --> Tracker : move
Old --> Tui : delete
Old --> Modes : delete
Old --> Local : delete
Old --> Terminal : delete
Old --> Packages : delete
Old --> Legacy : delete

note bottom of Port
HTTP Command API is the only host.
POST events keeps slash text as a user message.
CampusClaw owns Session names.
